CORE RULES

❌ NO ESTABLISHING SHOTS
❌ NO PEOPLE (NO silhouettes, NO reflections of bodies)
❌ NO STATIC FRAMES

✅ Camera always in motion (micro-drift minimum)
✅ Environment moves subtly even when “still”
✅ Memory ≠ reality (temporal bleed allowed)

WORLD LOGIC (LOCKED)
The train is operational, but the route has been erased
Infrastructure persists out of habit, not purpose
Time leaks through reflections, glass, sound
Snow functions as an eraser, not weather
Nothing breaks dramatically — it simply forgets

CAMERA LANGUAGE
POV-adjacent (as if remembered, not seen live)
Slight handheld inertia, like a body that isn’t there anymore
Focus breathes gently, never snaps
Motion is forward-biased but hesitant, as if unsure it’s allowed

0.0 – 1.2s - IN-MOTION ENTRY (NO START POINT)
Frame opens mid-glide.
Camera already drifting forward along the tracks — no acceleration phase.

Snow streaks subtly sideways, not downward.
Motion parallax confirms speed, but speed is indeterminate.

The skyline is already receding before the viewer realizes it.
Audio: electrical hum already present, as if it never began.

1.2 – 2.6s - TRACK MEMORY NOISE

Rails pass beneath camera with a faint rhythmic shimmer —
not mechanical, more like degraded tape flutter.

Snow on the sleepers vibrates inconsistently,
as if some frames remember motion and others don’t.

No hard forward thrust — motion feels permitted, not driven.

2.6 – 4.2s - TRAIN REVEAL (MOVING RELATIVE TO CAMERA)

The back of the train slides into frame from ahead —
not approached, but caught up to.

Camera speed slightly mismatched to train speed,
causing a gentle drift forward, then lag, then re-align.

Metal skin reflects ghost-light —
reflections trail behind camera motion by half a second.

4.2 – 6.0s - TEMPORAL DESYNC CONFIRMED

A window reflection shows passing structures that don’t exist anymore.
Older skyline geometry flickers only in reflection, never directly seen.

No cut.
Just a quiet disagreement between surfaces.

Audio: soft, distant PA static, not yet forming words.

6.0 – 8.0s

Tracks ahead subtly misalign for a single frame
Snow fills the gap immediately, hiding the error

8.0 – 10.0s

POV shifts closer to the train door window
Interior lights flicker on — empty seats visible for 0.5s
Lights shut off again

10.0 – 12.0s

Reflections in glass show motion behind the camera
—but when the camera eases back, nothing is there

12.0 – 14.0s

Snow begins falling upward
Very slowly
Only noticeable by rail accumulation reversing

14.0 – 16.0s

PA system activates softly:

“Next stop—”
Cut before destination is spoken

16.0 – 18.0s

City skyline flickers between two eras:
Modern towers
Then darker, lower structures
No glitch effect — purely optical

18.0 – 20.0s

Snow accumulates rapidly on the roof mid-shot
As if time fast-forwards for the environment only

20.0 – 23.0s

Train lights dim
Camera continues forward past the train
Tracks ahead dissolve under snow, leaving no direction

23.0 – 25.0s

Final POV drift into white snowfield
Wind fades
Electrical hum cuts abruptly

END ON SILENCE

